1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,700
At dawn, Lake Tana wakes in silence.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:06,940
Ethiopia's largest lake, the source of
the Blue Nile.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:13,120
For ages, tankwa paddlers have travelled
across this water.

4
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:16,031
The lake is their road and their home.

5
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:21,220
But hidden in the island forests are
ancient monasteries,

6
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:24,208
with a history that has crossed the
centuries.

7
00:00:25,725 --> 00:00:29,835
On their walls, saints appear in richly
coloured paintings.

8
00:00:29,835 --> 00:00:32,969
Every painting is both a prayer and a
lesson.

9
00:00:34,475 --> 00:00:36,652
Books written on parchment have kept
ancient

10
00:00:36,652 --> 00:00:38,632
knowledge and faith alive for centuries.

11
00:00:42,475 --> 00:00:47,408
By the light of beeswax tapers, scribes
wrote on parchment, letter by letter.

12
00:00:47,408 --> 00:00:49,906
Their patience can still be seen today.

13
00:00:51,475 --> 00:00:55,732
In times of war and hardship, these
treasures were kept safe on the islands.

14
00:00:55,732 --> 00:00:57,469
The waves could not erase them.

15
00:01:00,475 --> 00:01:02,363
Today this trust is in our hands.

16
00:01:02,363 --> 00:01:05,167
To know it, honour it and protect it is
our part.

17
00:01:08,475 --> 00:01:09,997
Tana is not only a beautiful lake.

18
00:01:09,997 --> 00:01:11,788
It is a story the waves could not erase,

19
00:01:11,788 --> 00:01:13,803
so let us protect it for the next
generation.
